I don't recall the details of that discussion. Typically I don't advance XL
deliberately (that is, if not necessary, for slots or quest admittance).
And which branches I take first depends on the concrete game. Making the
decision when to enter Sokoban depending on XL only because of the chance
that giants are maybe generated in the few squares where those scrolls of
earth are placed is a bit much, and IMO inappropriate as rule of thumb or
general strategy. YMMV.
If you want to blame the player then mostly because of what was one of my
suggestions to the OP upthread, and which I didn't think of at that moment:
>> Avoid combat with monsters if you know they possibly have picked up those
>> scrolls.
The scrolls are considered offensive items, but I have never seen them used
by monsters if you avoid melee.
OTOH, if I had avoided combat I wouldn't have been able to do Sokoban, since
the giants won't follow you downstairs, so the fight was inevitable anyway.
I seem to recall, though, that in my case the boulders were not all in the
corridor, so less a problem compared to the OP's situation.
An option would have been to come back later with some instant-death means.

